\subsection{Model Fitting}
\label{app:model fitting}
We create an additional "non active" state that serves as a mask to ensure all loan sequences cover the full dataset.
We sample loans in the following way in each batch: 
First, randomly pick a start time, then collect all active loans at that start time, and pick a subset N of them (set to 2500 in our experiments). We make this operation more efficient by first sorting the loans by origination date. 
Since the \setseq model uses a context window of 50 time steps we sample using overlap between the train, validation, and test sets and only compute train gradients and performance metrics on the masked indices within the respective partition. 
