The space $\tilde{M}_{Q}^{4}$ is homeomorphic to $\C P^{2}$. 

\end{thm}

\begin{rem}\label{T4MQ7}
Note that the symmetric power representation $T^4\to T^6$ gives free $T^3=T^4/\text{diag}(T^4)$-action on $M_{Q}^{7}$. 
For this action  in~\cite{BT1} we proved that $\C P^{5}/T^4 \cong S^2\ast \C P^2$, that is that $M_{Q}^{7}/T^4 \cong \C P^2$.
