 The coordinates  of the points of  the surface $M^{3}\subset M_{Q}^{5}\subset \R^8$ satisfy $v_2=v_4 = 0$ while $u_4, u_2\neq 0$.  This implies $v_1u_4=u_2v_3$,   $A=u_1u_4-u_2u_3$, $B=v_1u_4-u_2v_3$ and $u_1^2+v_1^2+u_3^2+v_3^2 +u_2^2 =\frac{1}{3}$.  In addition, 
