\label{sec:MCfermion}

This subsection presents results on the spectral density of the electrons at zero frequency. This is computed by digaonalizing $\mathcal{H}[f] + \mathcal{H}[c,f_1] + \mathcal{H}[c,f,f_1]$ in Eqs. (\ref{eq:fermionhop}), (\ref{Top2layers_Hamiltonian}), and (\ref{Yukawa}) for each sample in the Monte Carlo simulation of Section~\ref{sec:mc}, and averaging over the thermal ensemble in Eq.~(\ref{eq:Z20}).

First, in Fig.~\ref{fig:mascot}, we show results from the fermion-only computation of Ref.~\cite{Mascot22} in the normal state with no coupling to the fluctuations of the bosons $B$ and $U$, or to the fermionic spinons $f$.
