\subsection{Semi-Synthetic Data}
\label{subsec:sim_semi}
In the second experiment, we analyzed a multilayer network dataset collected by \citet{magnani2013}, which originally contained five layers describing social connections among $N=61$ employees at Aarhus University's Department of Computer Science. Three layers are obtained through surveys asking employees about regular working relationships (``Work"), repeated leisure activities (``Leisure"), and eating lunch together (``Lunch"). Two additional layers captured online Facebook friendships and publication co-authorship. Since the co-authorship network is almost fully contained within other layers \citep{magnani2013}, it was excluded from our analysis, leaving us with four unweighted and undirected networks.
Summary statistics for each layer are presented in Table~\ref{tab:network_stats}.
