Since $\stok{\mb{R}}{-1}$ is a singleton, refined convex $0-$polytope is just the singleton $\stok{\mb{A}}{0}$ itself. 
In general, refined $0-$polytopes of a higher dimensional space $\mb{A}$ are exactly finite subsets of $\stok{\mb{A}}{0} \simeq \mb{A}$. 

