For each test case, we evaluate the FLOP rate of the compute kernel by
calculating the ratio of the number of FLOPS in the untransformed
Algorithm~\ref{knl:action.vanilla} to the measured execution time. We
specifically use the untransformed kernel to compute the FLOPS. This choice is
made because transformations that utilize multiple work-items for the
computation within a cell involve recomputation of geometric factors,
leading to additional FLOPS that are not indicative of the net DOF-throughput,
which is a key factor in determining the computational efficiency for the
computational scientist.


To obtain the kernel execution time for a test case, we perform 5 warm-up
rounds, followed by measuring the wall clock timings of kernel runs until we
have at least 15 actual runs or a minimum total kernel runtime of 0.2 seconds.
The arithmetic mean of the kernel timing measurements is then computed.

