Since both the background component $\mathbf{B}_{\hat{\theta}}$ and the physical signal $\mathbf{S}_{\text{sim}}$ used to create the synthetic data are known, we can directly quantify the reconstruction accuracy of our method for each component. %This provides a controlled setting to better assess the performance of the proposed approach.
