\section{Conclusion}
We have shown how the fundamental problem of source separation from multiple source contributions can be approached from a fresh perspective by training a dual implicit neural representation. We demonstrate the utility and efficacy of our framework by applying it to a 4D inelastic neutron spectroscopy dataset, supplemented with simulations. In this way, we successfully extract  the single-magnon excitations from the inelastic neutron scattering data of a Mott insulator. This work provides a powerful and versatile framework for disentangling signals from multiple sources while simultaneously providing denoising and compression capabilities, contributing to the advancement of machine learning methods for scientific data analysis and source separation.

